      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of defining this FID in the pKVM range, I wonder if the \"SiP Service\" range would make more sense?\n\nThe spec describes it as\n\n\u003e Provides interfaces to SoC implementation-specific services on this platform, for example [...] some power control services\n\nand it seems more appropriate as\n\n- pKVM doesn\u0027t handle the HVC (it only monitors it)\n- the HVC could be conceptually tied to the CrosVM virtual platform:\n  - compatible with non-protected VMs\n  - compatible with current upstream Linux --\u003e driver could be upstreamed today\n  - (compatible with other hypervisors)\n  - guest potentially probes it as a `soc_device`\n- it doesn\u0027t introduce an exception to the potential rule that userspace should never attempt to handle FIDs in the pKVM range (see https://lore.kernel.org/all/20251201-smccc-filter-v2-1-03dab737a14d@google.com)\n\nWDYT?",
